        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T19:53:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that\u0027s the case. I would guess that if the default current for all ports is 3.0A then 3.0A can always be allocated and would always be allocated for each port in a source role. So the whole algorithm would be effectively be a no-op",
      "parentUuid": "603cad3a_d87bd7fa",
      "revId": "7a193859ea5dae50a342bc95ab7db16b1eca5b29",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
