        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T20:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the algorithm as defined here would work for all of our actual boards that default to 1.5A and can supply 3.0A to at most one port. But hypothetically, if you had a board that defaulted to 3.0 on a port, I think this would do something weird.\n\n3 lines down, the code removes `rem_non_pd` from `max_curent_claimed`. If the default current was in fact 3.0A, then the accounting in the bit fields in this file wouldn\u0027t match the actual current allocation. This policy could end up offering 3.0A on more ports than the board supported.\n\nIt\u0027s probably OK to wait for another CL to address this.",
      "parentUuid": "f8455f40_cdf12009",
      "revId": "7a193859ea5dae50a342bc95ab7db16b1eca5b29",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
