      "lineNbr": 3333,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T19:53:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this is called in an attached source state, then either the Rp value should be changed if it\u0027s a type-c only connection, or a new SRC_CAP should be sent if it\u0027s a USB-PD connection. The default Rp value should always track what was passed into this function. But, because pdc-\u003euna_policy is only checked if the port is in an unattached state, only setting the flag bit to force a write to the PDC if its unattached.",
      "parentUuid": "7d3574ae_dfccde00",
      "revId": "7a193859ea5dae50a342bc95ab7db16b1eca5b29",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "247acff2_12df3560",
