        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-06T20:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, this function will always update `una_policy.tcc`, which is the source of truth for the current limit to be applied. However, depending on the state, this function will set a different flag to trigger a different write to the PDC to implement the policy expressed in `tcc`, based on the current state?\n\nIs there any risk of that write not happening, because the state changed between the time that this function set the flag and the time that the state checked flags? Or would a state change override the effects of this function call anyway?",
      "parentUuid": "85999637_d3263a67",
